{"seconds": 53.1, "exit": 0, "final": "After Qc6+ Ke7 Qxa8, Black plays Qxa8 and material is equal. But after Qc6+ Qd7, White gets Qxa8+ and Black is still in check, winning the exchange (rook for nothing).\n\nSo the line is: **1.Qc6+ Qd7 2.Qxa8+** winning the rook.\n\nLet me verify this is the best move by checking if there are any better alternatives I missed. The key is that Qc6+ forces the queen to d7 (Ke7 also allows Qxa8), and then Qxa8+ wins material with check.\n\n**Best move:** Qc6+\n\n**Main line:** Qc6+ Qd7 Qxa8+ (winning rook)\n\n**Motif:** deflection (forcing the queen away from defending the rook)\n\n**Explanation:** Black's rook on a8 is undefended. White's queen on b7 controls key squares. By checking with Qc6+, White forces Black's queen to d7 to block, deflecting it from defending the rook. Then Qxa8+ wins the rook with check. After Ke7 instead of Qd7, Qxa8 still wins the rook because the queen on d8 cannot defend it. Always look for forcing moves that attack undefended pieces after moving the defender.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qc6+\", \"line\": [\"Qc6+\", \"Qd7\", \"Qxa8+\", \"Ke7\", \"Qxa7\"], \"motifs\": [\"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qc8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qe4+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qkbnr/pQp2ppp/8/8/3p4/8/PPP3PP/RNB1K2R w KQkq - 0 10", "move": "Qxa8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "r2qk